course: dictionary
lesson: 6880
title: Overnight: three meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Overnight can mean during the night, for the whole night, or very quickly. Read the words around it to see which one fits. «Breath smells in the morning because germs grow in the mouth overnight when there is less spit.» Germs grow while you sleep, so overnight here means during the night.
explain: The second meaning is about speed. An overnight success is someone who suddenly becomes famous, as if it happened in one night. «"Overnight" stars usually trained for years where nobody could see, like a tree that grows roots for a long time before anyone notices it above the ground.» The success looks sudden, but the hard work was slow and hidden.
explain: As an adjective, overnight describes a noun, such as an overnight bag or an overnight trip. It tells you the bag or the trip is for one night. Check by swapping in your meaning: does «an overnight bag» make sense as a bag for a night away? If yes, you have the right meaning.
fact: Overnight means during the night or for the whole night.
fact: Overnight can also mean very quickly or suddenly, as if in one night.
fact: As an adjective, overnight describes a noun, as in an overnight trip.
fact: «Overnight» can be used in a story to show that something changed surprisingly fast.
fact: Useful phrases: stay overnight, overnight bag, overnight trip, overnight success, leave overnight.
exercise: «Breath smells in the morning because germs grow in the mouth overnight when there is less spit.» What does overnight mean here? | Next to the bed | Before breakfast | *During the night | Very quickly, in a moment
exercise: Which phrase uses overnight as an adjective, describing a noun? | *An overnight trip | To stay overnight | Grew overnight | Left overnight by mistake
exercise: «"Overnight" stars usually trained for years where nobody could see.» What does overnight success suggest? | A trip that lasts one night | A star that falls from the sky | Something that happens while you are asleep only | *Sudden fame after years of hidden work
test: «In the desert God fed the people with manna, bread from heaven, enough for each day; kept overnight it went bad.» What does kept overnight mean? | *Stored for the whole night, until the morning | Thrown away at once | Cooked very quickly | Stored for the whole night
test: Mia says overnight only means sleeping. What is the best answer? | *No, it can also mean very quickly, as in an overnight success | No, it means only a short walk | Yes, it only ever means sleeping | Yes, but only in a desert
exam: In «an overnight bag», is overnight an adjective or an adverb? | Noun, because it names a place | Verb, because it shows an action | *Adjective, because it describes the bag | Adverb, because it describes how the bag was packed
